# A closure method (filter, map, any, fold) called on a temporary List or Map
# drops that receiver once the call returns. The fixture makes 300000 such
# calls, and its resident set grows by less than 8 MiB. If each receiver
# stayed alive, the growth would be tens of megabytes. A fold over a
# temporary evaluates its receiver once, so `produce` prints once. The
# result is the same at every tier.
fixture: a_temporary_receiver_of_a_closure_method_is_dropped_after_the_call.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step o0: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "steps 300000 total true\nresident growth under 8 MiB true\nreceiver made\nfold 6\n"
step o1: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "steps 300000 total true\nresident growth under 8 MiB true\nreceiver made\nfold 6\n"
step o2: jet run --release main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "steps 300000 total true\nresident growth under 8 MiB true\nreceiver made\nfold 6\n"
